{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on `a9ba0f7f`. Do not start the gate on `ff578887`. Point 3\nchanges source, and a gate on a head that changes after it is lost.\n\nPoint 3. The wait moves outside the fence. No call waits for the\nnetwork inside `store.exclusive`. Custody keeps that rule for a\ndelivery today (`packages/client/src/custody.ts:448`). The\nexploration reader can open a read session. A slow or lost answer\nthen holds every member call of every client that shares the\nstore: no edit, no dismiss, no submit of another slot.\n\nThe shape is yours, by the smaller change. Two forms meet the rule:\n- Explore first, outside the fence, on the candidate that the call\n  composes from an unfenced read. Then one fenced section reads\n  the batch, decides, checks `now`, composes the candidate again,\n  and requires that it equals the explored candidate.\n- Or two fenced sections with the exploration between them. The\n  second section reads the batch again and requires the same\n  stored draft and the same occurrence.\nIn each form a difference stops with `state`, and nothing signs. A\nmoved head alone is no difference: the scope judges the act.\n\nCases, in the existing owner:\n1. A reader that does not answer. While the submit waits, `edit`,\n   `dismiss` and a submit of another slot complete.\n2. The draft changes while the submit waits. When the reader\n   answers, the submit stops with `state`, signs nothing and\n   writes nothing.\n3. The reader answers and nothing changed: the submit signs one\n   time.\nAmend the read-cut text of the C4 note: a call decides on what it\nread under the fence, and a submit reads two times around its\nexploration.\n\nPoint 2. Yes, add the case of a return by an exploration before\nthe gate, with the `c4Runtime` fixture. It is the path where the\nadoption removes the stored cause: a stop before the signing\nleaves an editing draft with no return, and the next submit takes\nno `now` and explores.\n\nPoint 5d. Good: the scope refuses, so no act records without the\nbasis. The member then sees `bad-intent` for what is a race. Put\nthat in the note as a known wording limit. I add it to the E5\nrequest, where the pending source case already waits.\n\nThen the Node stage and one gate. Send the new head with START.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}